From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Thu, 4 Sep 2026 20:40:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] freedreno/a5xx: bracket GMEM passes with the CCU maintenance the vendor driver emits

A static reconstruction of the a540 vendor GL driver's tile loop (its
packets are rodata templates, so every event id is known) shows two
cache-maintenance events fd5 never emits in the GMEM path, both at
positions that bound the restore blit where an a540 lockup was decoded
(RB and UCHE busy, ME parked on the WFI after a tile's restore):

  - PC_CCU_INVALIDATE_COLOR and PC_CCU_INVALIDATE_DEPTH at the start of
    every GMEM pass, between the LRZ flush and the power/CCU setup.
    Without them, CCU lines the previous submit (on a5xx, frequently
    another process) left behind survive into the first restore.
  - PC_CCU_FLUSH_COLOR_TS, PC_CCU_FLUSH_DEPTH_TS and CACHE_FLUSH_TS at
    the end of the pass, before the UCHE invalidate; tile_fini only
    invalidates today, while the sysmem path already flushes the CCU.

Pure additions, matching the vendor's order.

Assisted-by: Claude
Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a5xx/fd5_gmem.c	2026-09-04 20:08:22.137190795 +0200
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a5xx/fd5_gmem.c	2026-09-04 20:31:19.226553418 +0200
@@ -393,6 +393,14 @@
    OUT_PKT7(ring, CP_SKIP_IB2_ENABLE_GLOBAL, 1);
    OUT_RING(ring, 0x0);
 
+   /* The vendor driver invalidates both CCU caches here, between the LRZ
+    * flush and the power/CCU setup, at the start of every GMEM pass; on
+    * a5xx nothing else clears lines the previous submit (another process)
+    * left behind before the first restore writes GMEM through the CCU.
+    */
+   fd5_event_write(batch, ring, PC_CCU_INVALIDATE_COLOR, false);
+   fd5_event_write(batch, ring, PC_CCU_INVALIDATE_DEPTH, false);
+
    OUT_PKT4(ring, REG_A5XX_PC_POWER_CNTL, 1);
    OUT_RING(ring, ctx->screen->info->num_sp_cores - 1); /* PC_POWER_CNTL */
 
@@ -691,6 +699,14 @@
 
    fd5_emit_lrz_flush(batch, ring);
 
+   /* Flush the CCU and the cache with timestamps before the UCHE
+    * invalidate, as the vendor driver does at the end of every GMEM pass;
+    * the sysmem path already does the CCU half of this in sysmem_fini.
+    */
+   fd5_event_write(batch, ring, PC_CCU_FLUSH_COLOR_TS, true);
+   fd5_event_write(batch, ring, PC_CCU_FLUSH_DEPTH_TS, true);
+   fd5_event_write(batch, ring, CACHE_FLUSH_TS, true);
+
    fd5_cache_flush(batch, ring);
    fd5_set_render_mode(batch->ctx, ring, BYPASS);
 }
